/*
   * Full-height chat/tool shell that sits under the app header.
   *
   * `100vh` on mobile browsers is the LARGE viewport — it's measured as if the
   * URL bar were retracted. So with the toolbar visible (the normal state) a
   * 100vh layout is taller than what you can actually see, and the bottom of
   * it — for the assistant, the message input — is pushed below the fold.
   * `100dvh` tracks the visible area as the toolbar shows and hides.
   *
   * The plain 100vh rule stays first as the fallback for anything that doesn't
   * know dvh; the @supports block wins everywhere that does (iOS Safari 15.4+,
   * Chrome 108+). In the native apps this matters less — Capacitor is
   * configured with Keyboard.resize: 'native', so the WebView itself shrinks —
   * but mobile web has no such help.
