/*
   * ELE-1752 — `--banner-height` is not optional padding.
   *
   * Announcement and maintenance banners render ABOVE the routed page, so they
   * push a viewport-sized shell down by their own height and an equal number
   * of pixels fall off the bottom. On the Elec-AI assistant the bottom is the
   * composer, and the shell does not scroll — so the input was simply gone
   * while an announcement was live. It defaults to 0px, so a page with no
   * banner is unchanged.
